# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for tests/cpp/*_stress.cpp (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...).
#
# hnswlib's insert holds the new node's link-list lock and takes each
# neighbour's in turn (addPoint -> searchBaseLayer / mutuallyConnectNewElement).
# Over many inserts every pair of nodes is taken in both orders, which TSan's
# deadlock detector reports as a lock-order inversion, even when every insert
# runs on one thread. DB::add runs under the exclusive mutex_, so two of those
# inserts never overlap; parallel_add (add_batch, open) uses upstream hnswlib's
# concurrent insertion. This suppresses only the lock-order report for these
# locks: data races are still reported everywhere.
deadlock:HierarchicalNSW<float>::addPoint
